# /terms and /refunds, retired 2026-08-16. They existed for one reason: Paddle's
# account review wants policy URLs on the seller's own domain, and perch was the
# thing that was going to be sold. perch went back to MIT with no paid tier on
# 2026-08-15 (hausfold/perch#67), and the user's decision the next day is that
# hausfold is not selling anything, ever — so the two pages described seats,
# renewals and a fourteen-day window for a licence that will never exist.
#
# Unlike every other retirement in this file, these have no successor page: no
# surface here carries what they carried, because what they carried is gone.
# They land on `/#apps`, the "Also from hausfold" paragraph, which is where the
# answer now lives ("Every one of them is free and open source: ... nothing to
# buy"). That sentence and that id were added in the same commit for exactly
# this reason — a redirect onto a page that doesn't answer the question is a
# soft 404, and bare `/` would leave the answer four sections below the fold.
# 🚨 `#apps` is therefore load-bearing in the same way `#desktops` is.
#
# They were published from 2026-08-08 and linked from /perch's colophon, and a
# policy URL outlives the policy, so they keep resolving forever.
/terms      /#apps  301
/terms/     /#apps  301
/refunds    /#apps  301
/refunds/   /#apps  301
